ber 39. Which digit is in the ones place?","choices":["10","7","9","8"],"correct_answer":2}]},{"quiz_id":"73f54f09-1026-559c-a0c7-6850aa37f443","topic_key":"g1-add-100","topic":"Addition with Sums up to 100","grade_level":1,"questions":[{"question":"A learner counts 12 safety cones and prepares 15 more. How many safety cones are there altogether?","choices":["27","25","26","28"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner needs 33 safety cones but already has 8. How many more safety cones are needed?","choices":["25","23","24","26"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner puts 5 safety cones in one group and 9 in another. Which number sentence shows the total correctly?","choices":["5 + 9 = 14","5 + 10 = 14","14 + 9 = 5","5 - 9 = 4"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner writes 26 + 26 in a record. Which expression has the same sum?","choices":["26 + 27","26 + 26","26 - 26","52 + 26"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner prepares 22 safety cones, then 9 more, and finally 7 more. How many are ready now?","choices":["38","37","39","36"],"correct_answer":0}]},{"quiz_id":"64ae5990-092b-5f8c-995f-9190a4481224","topic_key":"g1-pictographs","topic":"Pictographs and Data Tables","grade_level":1,"questions":[{"question":"A learner draws 4 stars in a pictograph. Each star represents 1 safety marker. How many safety markers are shown?","choices":["4","3","5","2"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner shows 6 stars for Monday and 3 for Tuesday. Each star represents 1 safety marker. How many more safety markers were recorded Monday?","choices":["3","4","1","2"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner shows 3 stars and 2 stars in two rows. Each star represents 1 safety marker. How many safety markers are represented altogether?","choices":["3","6","5","4"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner needs to represent 6 safety markers. Each star represents 1 safety marker. How many stars should be drawn?","choices":["6 stars","5 stars","4 stars","7 stars"],"co