r Tuesday. Each star represents 2 mangoes. How many more mangoes were recorded Monday?","choices":["3","1","2","0"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner shows 6 stars and 5 stars in two rows. Each star represents 10 mangoes. How many mangoes are represented altogether?","choices":["110","111","109","108"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner needs to represent 8 mangoes. Each star represents 2 mangoes. How many stars should be drawn?","choices":["4 stars","2 stars","5 stars","3 stars"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner transfers a row of 4 stars into a data table. Each star represents 2 mangoes. What value belongs in the table?","choices":["8 mangoes","6 mangoes","4 mangoes","10 mangoes"],"correct_answer":0}]},{"quiz_id":"979e2312-365e-5c84-97ca-a8f3b1b4cca0","topic_key":"g2-equal-groups","topic":"Multiplication Tables for 2, 3, 4, 5, and 10","grade_level":2,"questions":[{"question":"A learner arranges 2 equal groups with 3 counters in each group. How many counters are there?","choices":["8","6","4","2"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner fills 2 trays with 3 counters on each tray. What is the total?","choices":["9","0","3","6"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner makes 4 rows of 3 counters. Which multiplication sentence matches the array?","choices":["4 x 3 = 12","4 + 3 = 7","12 x 4 = 3","4 x 4 = 12"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner knows 5 x 5 = 25. What is 5 x 5?","choices":["20","15","25","30"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner needs 80 counters in equal groups of 10. How many groups are needed?","choices":["8","6","7","9"],"correct_answer":0}]},{"quiz_id":"6d081117-1bc7-52f9-aca3-82f287c85518","topic_key":"g2-division-tables","topic":"Division Using the 2, 3, 4, 5, and 10 Tables","grade_level":2,"questions":[{"question":"A learner shares 12 servings equally among 2 groups. How many go in each group?","choices":["7","5","4","6"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner packs 9 servings with 3 in each pack. How many packs are filled?","choices":["1","4","3","2"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner separates 15 servings into equal groups of 5. Which division sentence is correct?","choices":["15 ÷ 5 = 3","15 + 5 = 3","15 ÷ 3 = 15","5 ÷ 15 = 3"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner has 2 equal groups containing 10 servings each. Which total can be divided by 10 to get 2?","choices":["10","20","30","0"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner shares 9 store items equally among 3 groups. How many go in each group?","choices":["4","3","2","1"],"correct_answer":1}]},{"quiz_id":"7226e4f3-497c-5dd3-9bce-e48b1345b753","topic_key":"g2-odd-even","topic":"Odd and Even Numbers","grade_level":2,"questions":[{"question":"A learner counts 72 servings. Is 72 odd or even?","choices":["Odd","Even","Neither","Both"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner checks the numbers 30, 31, 33, 35. Which one is even?","choices":["31","30","33","35"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner needs the next even number after 75. Which number should be used?","choices":["74","75","77","76"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner needs the next odd number after 78. Which number should be used?","choices":["78","79","77","80"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner counts 94 store items. Is 94 odd or even?","choices":["Odd","Both","Neither","Even"],"correct_answer":3}]},{"quiz_id":"06297af6-0fa4-5364-a765-03d2194aca88","topic_key":"g2-fractions","topic":"Unit and Similar Fractions","grade_level":2,"questions":[{"question":"A learner divides a whole into 8 equal parts and selects 1 part. What unit fraction is selected?","choices":["0","1/8","1/4","1/9"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner compares 1/4 and 2/4 of two equal wholes. Which fraction is greater?","choices":["2/4","3/4","1/4","They are equal"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner uses 2 of 3 equal parts. What fraction of the whole is used?","choices":["1/2","1","2/3","1/3"],"correct_answer":2},{"questi