"choices":["Line segment","Flat surface","Ray","Circle"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner looks at a cylinder. Which surfaces does it have?","choices":["Only points","Only flat surfaces","No surface","Flat and curved surfaces"],"correct_answer":3}]},{"quiz_id":"804ef680-fe69-53ec-a9fd-0dc71fa4b729","topic_key":"g2-perimeter","topic":"Perimeter of Triangles, Squares, and Rectangles","grade_level":2,"questions":[{"question":"A learner marks a rectangular area 10 m long and 4 m wide. What is its perimeter?","choices":["30 m","26 m","24 m","28 m"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner places a square boundary with side length 5 m. What is the perimeter?","choices":["15 m","20 m","25 m","10 m"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner uses three fence sides measuring 11 m, 10 m, and 8 m for a triangle. What is the perimeter?","choices":["27 m","29 m","30 m","28 m"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner knows a rectangle has perimeter 30 m and length 8 m. What is its width?","choices":["6 m","8 m","7 m","5 m"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner walks around a 8-by-7 meter rectangular zone. How far is one complete trip around it?","choices":["30 m","31 m","29 m","28 m"],"correct_answer":0}]},{"quiz_id":"d547f2ae-c1cb-5dfb-9a33-c78a59103ea1","topic_key":"g3-area-rectangles","topic":"Area of Squares and Rectangles","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A learner plans a rectangular work area 10 m long and 5 m wide. What is its area?","choices":["45 m²","50 m²","40 m²","55 m²"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner marks a square area with side length 5 m. What is its area?","choices":["30 m²","15 m²","20 m²","25 m²"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner has a rectangular area of 24 m² with width 4 m. What is its length?","choices":["4 m","7 m","6 m","5 m"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner plans a rectangular work area 10 m long and 8 m wide. What is its area?","choices":["64 m²","88 m²","80 m²","72 m²"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner plans a rectangular work area 6 m long and 2 m wide. What is its area?","choices":["14 m²","8 m²","10 m²","12 m²"],"correct_answer":3}]},{"quiz_id":"fdd453c2-71ac-5d2b-83be-020646a0fcc6","topic_key":"g3-points-lines-rays","topic":"Points, Lines, Line Segments, and Rays","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A learner marks one exact position on a diagram. What geometric idea represents that position?","choices":["Line","Plane","Point","Ray"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner draws a straight path that extends forever in both directions. What is it?","choices":["Point","Line segment","Ray","Line"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner draws a straight path between Gate A and Gate B with both endpoints marked. What is it?","choices":["Ray","Plane","Line segment","Line"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner draws a figure that starts at one point and continues endlessly in one direction. What is it?","choices":["Ray","Point","Line segment","Circle"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner uses a flat map surface that extends in length and width. What geometric idea models it?","choices":["Ray","Plane","Point","Line segment"],"correct_answer":1}]},{"quiz_id":"8f7a5377-46eb-5e98-88fe-4817394eb504","topic_key":"g3-line-relationships","topic":"Parallel, Perpendicular, and Intersecting Lines","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A learner draws two lane lines that remain the same distance apart and never meet. What kind of lines are they?","choices":["Intersecting lines only","Parallel lines","Curved lines","Perpendicular lines"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner draws two paths that cross at a right angle. What kind of lines are they?","choices":["Rays only","Perpendicular lines","Curved lines","Parallel lines"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner draws two straight lines that cross but not at a right angle. What kind of lines are they?","choices":["No lines","Perpendicular lines","Intersecting lines","Parallel lines"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner checks opposite edges of a rectangle. What relationship do those edges have?","choices":["Curved","Perpendicular","Coincident only","Parallel"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner checks two adjacent sides of a square. What relationship do they have?","choices":["Perpendicular","Curved","Parallel","No relationship"],"correct_answer":0}]},{"quiz_id":"9971d390-c2b1-5d48-b1c2-77d6ff6ef2a0","topic_key":"g3-whole-numbers-10000","topic":"Whole Numbers up to 10,000","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A learner writes the number 2,687. What number comes immediately after it?","choices":["2,689","2,688","2,687","2,686"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner looks at the number 1,172. What number is 1 less than this label?","choices":["1,170","1,169","1,171","1,172"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner compares four numbers: 1,748, 1,756, 1,745, 1,761. Which is greatest?","choices":["1,745","1,756","1,748","1,761"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner must arrange 1,593, 1,594, 1,599 from smallest to largest. Which order is correct?","choices":["1,594 < 1,593 < 1,599","1,593 > 1,594 > 1,599","1,599 < 1,594 < 1,593","1,593 < 1,594 < 1,599"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner reads the counting pattern 3,170, 3,180, ___, 3,200, 3,210. Which number is missing?","choices":["3,170","3,180","3,190","3,200"],"correct_answer":2}]},{"quiz_id":"05b4941f-fab5-511e-9e34-409217fdaf05","topic_key":"g3-ordinals-100","topic":"Ordinal Numbers up to 100th","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A learner places a blue flower in position 4 of a line. How is that position written as an ordinal number?","choices":["4","4th","3rd","5th"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner stands at the 3rd place in a queue. What position comes immediately before it?","choices":["2nd","3rd","2","4th"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner calls the traveler immediately after the 5th position. Which position is called?","choices":["6","4th","5th","6th"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner checks a row where 3 flowers come before the red one. What is the red one's position?","choices":["3rd","4th","6th","5th"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner needs the last position among 6th, 7th, 8th, 9th. Which is last?","choices":["6th","7th","8th","9th"],"correct_answer":3}]},{"quiz_id":"149e159e-05be-5e77-a709-3158762002bf","topic_key":"g3-mass","topic":"Mass in Milligrams, Grams, and Kilograms","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A learner weighs cargo at 5 kilograms. How many grams is that?","choices":["5,000 g","3,000 g","6,000 g","4,000 g"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner weighs a very small paper tag. Which unit is most appropriate?","choices":["Meters","Liters","Milligrams","Kilograms"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner combines packages weighing 5000 g and 750 g. What is the total mass?","choices":["5,750 g","5,250 g","5,500 g","6,000 g"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner compares packages of 3 kg and 2 kg. What is their mass difference?","choices":["0 kg","3 kg","2 kg","1 kg"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner needs to split 7000 g equally into 7 packages. What is the mass of each package?","choices":["1,000 g","1,100 g","800 g","900 g"],"correct_answer":0}]},{"quiz_id":"5ba31f71-3df1-5ea7-8e77-709e2285d0bc","topic_key":"g3-capacity","topic":"Capacity in Milliliters and Liters","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A learner fills containers with 3 liters in all. How many milliliters is that?","choices":["3,000 mL","1,000 mL","2,000 mL","4,000 mL"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner measures one small cup of liquid. Which unit is most appropriate?","choices":["Kilograms","Kilometers","Milliliters","Meters"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner combines 3000 mL and 100 mL of liquid. What is the total capacity?","choices":["2,850 mL","2,600 mL","3,100 mL","3,350 mL"],"correct_answer":2},{