"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner removes 505 from a group of 1976 mangoes. Which number sentence is correct?","choices":["1,976 + 505 = 2,481","1,976 - 1,471 = 1,471","1,976 - 505 = 1,471","505 - 1,976 = 1,471"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner has ₱3,500 and spends ₱1,275. How much money remains?","choices":["₱2,125","₱2,225","₱2,325","₱4,775"],"correct_answer":1}]},{"quiz_id":"9dda8fdb-6985-590b-8dbe-7a3a9a796ab6","topic_key":"g3-bar-graphs","topic":"Tables and Single Bar Graphs","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A bar graph shows Mon = 8, Tue = 10, Wed = 9, and Thu = 7. Which day has the greatest value?","choices":["Wednesday","Monday","Tuesday","Thursday"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner records a table: Mon=16, Tue=20, Wed=16, Thu=17. What is the total for all four days?","choices":["59","69","64","74"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner shows graph values 18, 14, 20, 19. What is the difference between the highest and lowest values?","choices":["7","5","6","4"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner looks at a graph where Mon has value 11. Which table entry matches it?","choices":["Mon - 10","Tue - 11","Mon - 11","Mon - 12"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner looks at a graph where Tue has value 15. Which table entry matches it?","choices":["Tue - 14","Tue - 15","Wed - 15","Tue - 16"],"correct_answer":1}]},{"quiz_id":"e4144882-dc1e-5e27-95a7-de9476400fef","topic_key":"g3-likelihood","topic":"Likelihood of Outcomes","grade_level":3,"questions":[{"question":"A learner draws one ticket from a bag containing only blue tickets. How likely is a blue ticket?","choices":["Equally likely","Certain","Impossible","Unlikely"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner draws a red ticket from a bag containing no red tickets. How likely is this event?","choices":["Certain","Equally likely","Likely","Impossible"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner draws from a bag with 1 gold ticket and 9 blue tickets. How 