"4d311cb2-4a83-53d1-a6e3-fd0cffc37985","topic_key":"g5-volume","topic":"Cubes and Rectangular Prisms","grade_level":5,"questions":[{"question":"A learner checks a cube with edge 8 cm. What is its volume?","choices":["384 cm³","512 cm³","576 cm³","448 cm³"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner checks a box 9 cm long, 3 cm wide, and 3 cm high. What is its volume?","choices":["72 cm³","81 cm³","63 cm³","90 cm³"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner knows a box volume is 600 cm³, with length 12 cm and width 10 cm. What is its height?","choices":["5 cm","4 cm","6 cm","3 cm"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner fills a rectangular space with unit cubes in 8 layers of 3 by 2. How many unit cubes fit?","choices":["36 cubes","48 cubes","42 cubes","54 cubes"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner checks a box 7 cm long, 3 cm wide, and 3 cm high. What is its volume?","choices":["72 cm³","45 cm³","54 cm³","63 cm³"],"correct_answer":3}]},{"quiz_id":"92030069-1ece-5730-903f-f31166b84c30","topic_key":"g5-rotation","topic":"Rotation about a Point","grade_level":5,"questions":[{"question":"A learner rotates a point 90 degrees clockwise about the origin from (2, 3). Where does it land?","choices":["(2, 3)","(-2, -3)","(-3, 2)","(3, -2)"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner rotates a point 90 degrees counterclockwise about the origin from (4, 1). Where does it land?","choices":["(-1, 4)","(4, 1)","(1, -4)","(-4, -1)"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner rotates point (3, -2) by 180 degrees about the origin. Where does it land?","choices":["(-2, 3)","(3, 2)","(2, -3)","(-3, 2)"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner turns a sign one quarter turn clockwise. How many degrees is the rotation?","choices":["360 degrees","180 degrees","45 degrees","90 degrees"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner turns a marker three quarter turns clockwise. What single counterclockwise turn gives the same final position?","choices":["One half turn","Three quarter turns","One quarter turn","One full turn"],"correct_answer":2}]},{"quiz_id":"efd10051-001e-597e-bd72-1a3782f1fb6b","topic_key":"g6-tessellation","topic":"Tessellation of Shapes","grade_level":6,"questions":[{"question":"A learner covers a floor using equal squares with no gaps or overlaps. What pattern is formed?","choices":["Number line","Tessellation","Single reflection","Open curve"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner chooses a regular shape that tessellates by itself. Which one works?","choices":["Regular heptagon","Equilateral triangle","Circle","Regular pentagon"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner chooses another regular shape that tessellates by itself. Which one works?","choices":["Circle","Regular hexagon","Oval","Regular pentagon"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner checks a design made of circles placed side by side. Why is it not a tessellation?","choices":["It has colors","It uses equal shapes","It repeats","It leaves gaps"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner repeats a tile by sliding it right with no turning. Which transformation builds the pattern?","choices":["Reflection only","Division","Translation","Enlargement"],"correct_answer":2}]},{"quiz_id":"19dbbf20-bcaf-5fc0-8f8a-e6fb1c3624eb","topic_key":"g6-transformations","topic":"Translation, Reflection, and Rotation","grade_level":6,"questions":[{"question":"A learner slides a figure 4 units right without turning it. What transformation is this?","choices":["Reflection","Translation","Dilation","Rotation"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner flips a figure over a line. What transformation is this?","choices":["Rotation","Reflection","Translation","Tessellation"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner turns a figure 90 degrees about a fixed point. What transformation is this?","choices":["Reflection","Enlargement","Translation","Rotation"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner applies a translation, reflection, or rotation. Which property is preserved?","choices":["Area becomes zero","Size and shape","Only position","Only color"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner maps point (2, 5) to (-2, 5). Which transformation across an axis occurred?","choices":["Reflection across the x-axis","Reflection across the y-axis","Translation up","90-degree rotation"],"correct_answer":1}]},{"quiz_id":"c6d68697-d163-556d-9766-37c0080bf629","topic_key":"g6-decimal-operations","topic":"Four Operations with Decimals","grade_level":6,"questions":[{"question":"A learner combines decimal quantities 19 and 10.01. What is their sum?","choices":["28.81","29.01","29.11","28.91"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner subtracts 17.77 from 18.11. What is the difference?","choices":["0.44","0.24","0.14","0.34"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner calculates 6.9 x 0.3 for a work record. What is the product?","choices":["2.17","2.07","1.87","1.97"],"correct_answer":1},{"question":"A learner divides 47.6 equally by 7. What is the quotient?","choices":["6.9","6.7","6.8","6.6"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner evaluates 2.6 + 2.1 x 5. What is the result?","choices":["12.6","13.1","13.6","12.1"],"correct_answer":1}]},{"quiz_id":"a1c52c4a-d072-5c27-88e3-8154bdd0ef62","topic_key":"g6-fraction-operations","topic":"Operations with Fractions, Whole Numbers, and Mixed Numbers","grade_level":6,"questions":[{"question":"A learner multiplies 2 1/4 by 1/2. What is the product?","choices":["1 1/8","1 1/4","2 1/8","4 1/2"],"correct_answer":0},{"question":"A learner divides 4 1/4 by 1/2. What is the quotient?","choices":["2 1/8","4 3/4","8 1/2","9"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner calculates 1 1/2 x 3/4 for a supply record. What is the result?","choices":["8/9","1","1 1/8","1 1/4"],"correct_answer":2},{"question":"A learner calculates 3 3/4 ÷ 1/4 for a supply record. What is the result?","choices":["7 1/2","16","14","15"],"correct_answer":3},{"question":"A learner multiplies 4 1/2 by 4. What is the product?","choices":["